+## beforeSession failure semantics
+
+- `beforeSession` runs inside the turn's `try` block, so a throw from it reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller still receives the rejection unchanged, `onError` fires with that error in the same argument shape as any other orchestrator failure (still behind the `catch`'s `instanceof Error` gate, recorded below), and `afterSession` still fires, so the release half of an allocate-in-`beforeSession` / release-in-`afterSession` pair runs on exactly the path where the allocation failed ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- On that path a hook can assume the turn was aborted before any user-input rewriting, provider interaction or tool execution, and that the session's entries are exactly as the caller handed them over. The engine deliberately keeps `afterSession` unconditional and tells no hook why the turn ended, so `afterSession` cannot distinguish a failed `beforeSession` from a completed one — a deployer who needs that distinction records it across its own hook pair ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
